---
// Shared sticky shell for Header.astro (doc pages) and LandingHeader.astro (landing + 404): owns
// the grid layout, translucent + blurred background, and hairline bottom border, so the two
// page-specific headers can't drift on those properties again. Header-specific content (brand,
// search, nav) is passed through the default slot.
//
// Sticky at every breakpoint: the sidebar and TOC rails stick to `top: var(--header-height)` (see
// SidebarNav/Toc), so this has to stay put for them to tuck under it.
//
// Translucent + blurred so a code block or table scrolling underneath reads through softly rather
// than vanishing behind a hard edge. `@supports` falls back to the previous opaque `var(--bg)` on
// engines without backdrop-filter, where the see-through color alone would be unreadable against
// busy content.
---

<header class="header-shell">
	<slot />
</header>

<style>
	.header-shell {
		position: sticky;
		top: 0;
		z-index: 20;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: var(--rail-width) 1fr;
		height: var(--header-height);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-08);
		background: var(--bg);
	}

	@supports (backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) or (-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) {
		.header-shell {
			background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 72%, transparent);
			-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px) saturate(1.15);
			backdrop-filter: blur(12px) saturate(1.15);
		}
	}

	/* Tablet: the left rail column is gone (SidebarNav narrows in place, but nothing needs to
	   align with it up here), so this becomes a plain flex row: logo, search, repo link,
	   hamburger. */
	@media (max-width: 1023px) {
		.header-shell {
			display: flex;
			align-items: center;
			gap: 18px;
			padding: 0 26px;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 767px) {
		.header-shell {
			gap: 12px;
			padding: 0 18px;
		}
	}
</style>
